    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0078" n="68" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg68"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 E.A.C./10–1644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18638</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-16">October 16,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received October 21.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous despatches
                    transmitting replies from various interested Allied Governments<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d48-f1"/> to the letter of July 25, 1944, from the Chairman of the
                    European Advisory Commission, I have the honor to submit two reports on the
                    views of the above mentioned Allied Governments which were prepared by a
                    Committee of Experts of the three Delegations.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the reports cover only certain aspects of the surrender of
                    Germany. They do not cover subjects which the Commission plans to incorporate in
                    general orders and directives.</p>
                <p>In view of the unwillingness of the Soviet Delegation to examine the reply
                    submitted by the Polish Government, a separate report has been prepared by the
                    United States and British Delegations with respect to the Polish
                        memorandum.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d48-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador: <lb/>
                    <signed>E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Allan Lightner, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary, U.S. Delegation European Advisory
                        Commission</hi>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d48-a1.xml" xpointer="d48-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d48-a2.xml" xpointer="d48-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d48-f1" n="54" xml:id="d48-f1-content">
